{title: 367 - Rescue the Perishing}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Church}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Bb]Rescue the perishing,
[Bb]Care [Eb]for [F]the [Bb/F]dying;
[F/C]Snatch [C7]them in [F7]pity [Bb]from sin and the grave;
[Bb]Weep [Eb]o’er the [F]erring [Bb]one,

Refrain:
[Eb]Rescue [F]the perishing, care for [Bb]the dying;
[F]Jesus [Bb]is merciful, Jesus [F7]will save.

Verse 2:
[Bb]Though they are slighting him, still he is waiting,
[Bb]waiting [Eb]the penitent [F]child to [Bb/F]receive;
[F/C]plead with [C7]them earnestly, [Bb]plead with them gently;
[Bb]he [Eb]will forgive [Bb]if [F]they only [Bb/F]believe.

Verse 3:
[Bb]Rescue the perishing, duty demands it;
[Bb]strength [Eb]for thy labor [F]the Lord will [Bb/F]provide;
[F/C]back to [C7]the narrow [Bb]way patiently win them;
[Bb]tell [Eb]the poor wanderer [F]a Savior [Bb]has died.
